## gotransit context

This is a Next.js monorepo for the Metrolinx GO Transit website. The project uses TypeScript, react-hook-form for form validation, and jest for testing. The specific work is on the CheckoutForm component at src/components/pages/CheckoutPage — a form for transit fare purchases that validates email address confirmation with case-sensitive matching (TRM774 requirement).

Key commands and facts:
- `npm test` runs jest; the component has a spec file at src/components/pages/CheckoutPage/__tests__/CheckoutForm.spec.tsx alongside CheckoutForm.tsx
- `npm run lint` runs eslint; `npm run type-check` runs tsc for TypeScript checking (inferred from a Next.js/TypeScript project)
- Pre-commit hooks (husky + lint-staged) enforce a branch naming regex (^(feature|bugfix|tech|release|hotfix)/[a-zA-Z0-9.-]+(/[a-z0-9-]+)?$) and run commitlint on commit messages
- The validation logic lives in react-hook-form's resolver and register patterns; TRM774 marks the email confirm check
- Test coverage for the validation rules is incomplete and must be extended alongside code changes

When checking claims: verify that files exist at stated paths, that validation changes use react-hook-form patterns, and that test expectations match actual component behavior. Do not assume symlinks or dynamic imports resolve as written without checking.

